===Etymology 2===

====Verb====
{{head|ru|verb form}}

# {{inflection of|ru|быть||||pres|ind}}
# [[there is]], [[there are]], [[exists]]/[[exist]] {{gl|expresses availability, existence or presence}}
#: {{ant|ru|нет}}
#: {{uxi|ru|в э́той газе́те '''есть''' интере́сная статья́|there is an interesting article in this newspaper}}
# am/is/are located (at) (usually omitted)
# {{n-g|used to express possession}}
#: {{uxi|ru|у меня́ '''есть''' вопро́с|I have a question}}
# [[am]], [[is]], [[are]] (used with any person or thing in any number, usually omitted but used for emphasis)
#: {{uxi|ru|кто ты '''есть'''?|who are you (at all)?}}

====Usage notes====
* This form of {{m|ru|быть}} is special and most frequently used in the present tense, for past and future tense and other forms, see {{m|ru|быть}}.
* The pre-reform orthography (1918) form {{m|ru|ѣсть}} doesn't apply to this sense, only to the sense "to eat", thus the two terms were spelled differently before the reform.

===Etymology 3===
Borrowed from {{bor|ru|en|yes}}.

